/* Readings for secondary progressions, solar returns and dominant planets. */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};

window.AstroDeep.progressions = {
  intro: "Secondary progressions are one of the oldest timing tools in astrology, built on a simple rule: each day after your birth stands for one year of your life. The sky on the day you turned ten days old describes the inner weather of your tenth year, the sky thirty days after birth describes your thirtieth, and so on. Because the planets move slowly by this measure, the progressed chart unfolds gently, like a photograph developing over decades.\n\nWhere transits often coincide with outside events, progressions describe what is maturing inside you. They show shifts in mood, identity, taste and priorities that you may only recognise in hindsight. A progressed Moon changing sign can feel like a change of emotional season, while a progressed Sun changing sign can mark a quiet rewrite of who you think you are. Read them as the story of your inner development, not a list of things that will happen to you.",

  moonSigns: {
    aries: "With the progressed Moon in Aries you enter an emotional chapter of about two and a half years that wants a fresh start. Patience wears thin, and you may feel restless with arrangements that once felt comfortable. This is a time to act on instinct, start something on your own terms and notice where you have been waiting for permission. Anger can surface more quickly than usual, often pointing to a need you have ignored. Used well, this period rebuilds your courage and reminds you that you are allowed to want things for yourself.",
    taurus: "The progressed Moon in Taurus slows the emotional pace and asks you to settle. For roughly two and a half years, comfort, security and the body take priority. You may find yourself caring more about money, home, food, gardens or simple routines that steady you. After a busier chapter this can feel like exhaling. The risk is getting stuck, holding on to what is familiar because change feels too costly. The gift is a deep sense of what you truly value, and the patience to build something that lasts.",
    gemini: "When the progressed Moon moves into Gemini your mind wakes up. This chapter of about two and a half years brings curiosity, conversation, short trips, new courses and a hunger for information. You may feel lighter and more sociable, happy to sample many things rather than commit to one. Siblings, neighbours and local connections can become more important. Emotionally you process by talking and writing, so journals and good friends help. Watch for scattered energy and nervous overthinking, and let this be a season of learning without pressure to decide. A notebook by the bed is not a bad idea.",
    cancer: "The progressed Moon in Cancer is at home, and for about two and a half years your emotional life turns inward and toward the people you belong to. Family, home, parenting, ancestry and the need to feel safe move to the centre. You may move house, renovate, care for a relative or simply want more time in your own nest. Old memories and childhood feelings can surface to be understood. Sensitivity runs high, so protect your energy. This chapter teaches you how to nurture yourself as well as you nurture others. Say yes to invitations that feel like home.",
    leo: "With the progressed Moon in Leo you want to be seen. This roughly two and a half year chapter brings a need for joy, play, creativity and recognition. You may take up a creative project, fall in love, spend more time with children or step into a more visible role. Your heart is more open and more generous, and it also bruises more easily when attention is withheld. Let yourself enjoy things without justifying them. The lesson is to express yourself warmly and fully, rather than waiting to be invited onto the stage.",
    virgo: "The progressed Moon in Virgo brings an emotional chapter of about two and a half years focused on improvement. You may want to sort out your health, daily routines, work habits or the clutter around you. Feeling useful becomes deeply satisfying, and there can be a strong urge to learn a practical skill or serve others. The shadow is worry and self-criticism, a sense that nothing you do is quite enough. Direct that sharp eye toward systems rather than yourself, and this becomes a quietly healing and productive season.",
    libra: "When the progressed Moon enters Libra, relationships take centre stage for roughly two and a half years. You feel the need for partnership, fairness and beauty, and you may enter, deepen or renegotiate a significant bond. Loneliness can feel sharper, and so can the pull to keep the peace at any price. This is a good chapter for learning how to cooperate without losing yourself. Art, design and pleasant surroundings soothe you. Notice where you have been bending too far, and practise asking for balance out loud.",
    scorpio: "The progressed Moon in Scorpio takes you into deep emotional water for about two and a half years. Feelings intensify, and you may face questions of trust, intimacy, power, money shared with others or loss. What has been hidden tends to come up, sometimes uncomfortably, but always with the chance to heal it properly. You may crave privacy and honesty in equal measure. This is a powerful time for therapy, research or any work that goes beneath the surface. You come out of it more resilient and less afraid of your own depths.",
    sagittarius: "With the progressed Moon in Sagittarius your emotional life opens up. For roughly two and a half years you want space, meaning and adventure. Travel, study, spiritual exploration or a change of outlook can feel essential rather than optional. You may grow impatient with anything that feels small or confining. Optimism returns after heavier chapters, and you are more willing to take a chance. Watch a tendency to run from difficult feelings by staying busy. Let this be a season of broadening your horizons and finding your own philosophy.",
    capricorn: "The progressed Moon in Capricorn brings a serious, purposeful emotional chapter of about two and a half years. You may take on more responsibility, focus on career goals or feel pressure to prove yourself. Feelings can go underground while you get on with the job, and some people experience this period as lonely or heavy. It is also deeply strengthening. You learn what you can carry, and you build structures that support you for years. Remember to rest, and let others see the effort behind your composure.",
    aquarius: "When the progressed Moon moves into Aquarius you want freedom and a little distance. This two and a half year chapter often brings new friendships, group involvement, community causes or an interest in technology and new ideas. You may feel less bound by old emotional patterns and more willing to live unconventionally. Some people feel detached for a while, observing their feelings rather than drowning in them. That distance can be useful. The invitation is to rethink how you want to live and who you want around you. Expect your circle of friends to change shape.",
    pisces: "The progressed Moon in Pisces completes the emotional cycle and brings a softer, more porous chapter of about two and a half years. Sensitivity, intuition and imagination increase, and you may feel drawn to rest, retreat, art, music or spiritual practice. Endings are common, as old attachments quietly dissolve to make space for the next cycle. Boundaries can blur, so watch for exhaustion or escapism. This is a time to forgive, grieve what needs grieving and trust that something new is gestating beneath the surface.",
  },

  moonHouses: {
    1: "As the progressed Moon crosses your first house, your feelings sit right on the surface. You are more visible, more reactive and more aware of how you come across. This is often a time of personal reinvention: a new look, new habits or a stronger sense of what you need for yourself. Others notice your moods quickly. Use this period to put your own needs first for a while and to show up as you actually are. A haircut, a new wardrobe or a fitness goal can mark the shift.",
    2: "With the progressed Moon in your second house, emotional security links closely to money, possessions and self-worth. You may focus on earning, saving or reorganising your finances, and spending can become a way to soothe feelings. This is a good time to ask what you truly value and whether your resources reflect it. Building a steady income or a comfortable home base can bring real peace of mind. Notice which purchases genuinely comfort you and which are simply filling a gap. A small emergency fund can do more for your nerves this year than any treat.",
    3: "The progressed Moon moving through your third house makes your mind busy and your days full of conversation. Writing, learning, short trips, siblings and neighbours can all become emotionally important. You may take a course, start a blog or simply talk things through more than usual. Restlessness is common. Let curiosity lead, and notice how putting feelings into words helps you understand them. A regular walk around your neighbourhood can become an unexpected source of calm.",
    4: "When the progressed Moon reaches your fourth house, home and family become the emotional centre of life. You might move, renovate, start a family or care for a parent. Old family patterns and childhood memories often resurface to be looked at with adult eyes. You may want more privacy and quiet. This is a time for putting down roots and building a foundation that genuinely supports you. You may find yourself looking through old photographs or asking older relatives questions you never thought to ask. The answers can explain a great deal about you.",
    5: "The progressed Moon in your fifth house brings a desire for joy, romance, play and creative expression. Children may feature strongly, whether your own or others'. You are more willing to take emotional risks and to follow what delights you. Hobbies can turn into passions. Let yourself have fun without needing it to be productive, and notice what makes your heart feel alive. Dancing, painting, singing or simply laughing more are all fair uses of this time. Pay attention to who and what makes you feel most like yourself.",
    6: "With the progressed Moon crossing your sixth house, daily routines, health and work demand attention. You may change jobs, rethink your schedule or start caring for your body more deliberately. Stress tends to show up physically, so listen to it. Feeling useful matters a great deal now. Small, steady improvements to your habits can have a surprisingly large effect on your emotional wellbeing. Pets, co-workers and the rhythm of an ordinary Tuesday can matter more than you expect. Build a day you can live with happily.",
    7: "As the progressed Moon moves through your seventh house, partnership becomes the main emotional arena. You may marry, commit, separate or renegotiate a close relationship. Business partners and close collaborators also matter more. You learn about yourself through other people now, sometimes by seeing your own patterns reflected back. Aim for relationships where needs flow both ways. If you tend to give more than you receive, this is the period when that habit becomes impossible to ignore. Honest conversations now can make a partnership much stronger.",
    8: "The progressed Moon in your eighth house takes feelings deeper. Intimacy, trust, shared money, inheritance, debt or loss can come into focus. You may confront fears or long-buried emotions, and the experience can be transformative. This is a strong period for therapy, honest conversations and letting go of what no longer serves you. Vulnerability becomes a source of strength rather than a threat. Joint finances, wills or shared property may also need sorting out. Handling them with care brings unexpected relief.",
    9: "With the progressed Moon in your ninth house you need to grow beyond familiar horizons. Travel, higher study, spiritual exploration, publishing or contact with other cultures can feed you emotionally. Your beliefs may shift as experience teaches you something new. You feel more optimistic and more restless. Follow the questions that excite you, and let your worldview expand. A long trip, a degree or a mentor from a different background can change the way you see your whole life.",
    10: "The progressed Moon crossing your tenth house brings career, reputation and public life to the emotional foreground. You may take on a more visible role, reach a professional milestone or feel strong pressure to achieve. How the world sees you matters more now. Make sure your ambitions reflect what you actually care about, not just what others expect of you. You may also become more aware of your mother or another key parent figure as a role model. Decide which parts of their example you want to keep and which you are ready to leave behind.",
    11: "As the progressed Moon moves through your eleventh house, friendships, groups and hopes for the future become important. You may join a community, find your people or rethink which friendships still fit. Long-term goals come into sharper focus. This is a sociable, forward-looking period. Invest in networks that share your values, and let yourself dream a little bigger. A club, a cause or an online community might become an unexpected second home. Your social life can change shape considerably, and that is part of the point.",
    12: "The progressed Moon in your twelfth house brings a quieter, more inward chapter. You may need more solitude, rest and reflection, and old emotional material can surface for healing. Endings are common as one cycle closes. Spiritual practice, creative work and service to others can be deeply nourishing. Treat this as a gestation period, preparing you for the fresh start that follows. Sleep, dreams and time near water can all be restorative. Let yourself move more slowly than the world around you for a while.",
  },

  sunSigns: {
    aries: "The progressed Sun in Aries opens a roughly thirty year chapter in which your identity grows bolder and more self-directed. You become more willing to lead, compete and start things from scratch. Where you once waited for approval, you now learn to act first. This chapter builds courage and independence. The lesson is to assert yourself without bulldozing others, and to trust that your own initiative is enough to begin. You may take up a sport, start a business or simply stop apologising for your ambitions. Energy tends to rise, and so does impatience, so learn to pace yourself for the long run.",
    taurus: "With the progressed Sun in Taurus, a thirty year chapter of steadiness and consolidation begins. Your sense of self becomes grounded in what you can build, own and enjoy. Security, comfort and sensual pleasure matter more, and you grow more patient. This period rewards persistence and careful investment of time and money. The challenge is avoiding stubbornness when life asks you to adapt. Many people buy land or a home during this chapter, or put down roots in a place that finally feels right. Your voice, your body and your sense of pleasure all ask for attention.",
    gemini: "When the progressed Sun enters Gemini, your identity grows more curious, flexible and communicative for about thirty years. You may become a writer, teacher, connector or perpetual student. Variety feeds you, and you are more comfortable holding several interests at once. This chapter sharpens your mind and widens your social circle. The work is learning to go deep enough that your ideas take root. You may change careers more than once, or find a role that lets you use many skills at once. Friendships with siblings or peers can become more important too.",
    cancer: "The progressed Sun in Cancer turns your sense of identity toward home, family and emotional belonging for roughly thirty years. Caring for others, creating a safe base and honouring your roots become central to who you are. You may grow more protective and more sensitive. This chapter deepens your capacity to nurture. The lesson is to let yourself be cared for too, rather than only giving. You may find yourself becoming the person who holds the family together, or creating a chosen family of your own. Your instincts about people grow sharper and more reliable.",
    leo: "With the progressed Sun in Leo, a thirty year chapter of self-expression begins. You are more willing to shine, create and take up space. Recognition, love and creative achievement become important to your sense of self. Many people find their confidence here after years of holding back. The challenge is to lead from the heart rather than from a need for applause, and to encourage others to shine as well. You may take up performing, teaching or leading in some visible way. Children, whether your own or those you mentor, often play a part in this chapter.",
    virgo: "The progressed Sun in Virgo brings a roughly thirty year chapter focused on mastery, service and refinement. Your identity grows through useful work, skill and attention to detail. Health and daily routines often become more important. You may develop real expertise in a craft. The risk is an inner critic that never switches off. Learn to value progress over perfection, and your competence becomes a gift to many. Many people change their diet, working pattern or approach to health in lasting ways. You find deep pleasure in doing ordinary things really well.",
    libra: "When the progressed Sun moves into Libra, relationships and fairness shape your identity for about thirty years. You become more diplomatic, more aesthetic and more aware of other people's perspectives. Partnership may define much of this chapter, in love or in work. You learn the art of collaboration. The deeper lesson is to keep your own centre while seeking harmony, rather than disappearing into what others want. Your taste becomes more refined, and you may develop an interest in design, law or mediation. Fairness stops being an abstract idea and becomes a daily practice.",
    scorpio: "The progressed Sun in Scorpio opens an intense, transformative thirty year chapter. Your identity deepens as you face questions of power, intimacy, trust and change. Surface-level living stops satisfying you. You may be drawn to psychology, research, healing or any work that uncovers what is hidden. This period can include profound endings and rebirths. It leaves you with emotional strength and very little patience for pretence. You grow more comfortable with silence, secrets and strong feelings. Close relationships become either much deeper or clearly over.",
    sagittarius: "With the progressed Sun in Sagittarius, your identity expands for roughly thirty years. You seek meaning, adventure and a bigger picture. Travel, study, teaching or spiritual exploration can become central, and you grow more candid and optimistic. This chapter asks you to live by your own philosophy. The challenge is following through on your enthusiasm and remembering that other people's truths matter too. You may live abroad, gain a qualification or find a spiritual practice that anchors you. Your sense of humour often grows along with your sense of adventure.",
    capricorn: "The progressed Sun in Capricorn begins a thirty year chapter of ambition, responsibility and long-term achievement. Your identity becomes tied to what you build and the authority you earn. You grow more disciplined and more realistic, often taking on leadership. This period rewards patience and integrity. The lesson is to measure success by your own standards and to allow warmth alongside the hard work. Status and structure matter more, and you may take on roles that others rely on. Your relationship with time changes: you plan further ahead and value what endures.",
    aquarius: "When the progressed Sun enters Aquarius, your identity grows more independent and forward-thinking for about thirty years. You may question conventions, embrace unusual interests or find purpose in community and social change. Friendships and group work become important. This chapter frees you from roles that no longer fit. The challenge is staying emotionally present while you pursue your ideals. You may embrace technology, activism or an unusual lifestyle. Your friendships often become more diverse, and you care less about fitting in.",
    pisces: "The progressed Sun in Pisces opens a roughly thirty year chapter of sensitivity, imagination and spiritual depth. Your sense of self becomes softer and more compassionate, and you may be drawn to art, healing, music or service. Rigid goals matter less than meaning and connection. This period can dissolve old identities. The lesson is to keep healthy boundaries while trusting the intuition that now guides you. Retreats, creative work or caring roles may become important. You learn that softness and strength are not opposites.",
  },

  phases: {
    "New Moon": "The progressed New Moon starts a fresh 29.5 year cycle, and the three and a half years that follow feel like planting seeds in the dark. You may not know yet what you are starting, only that the old story no longer fits. Instinct is more reliable than planning now. Try new things, follow unexpected interests and notice what keeps drawing you back. The seeds you plant in this phase shape the next three decades, so choose them with care. Keep a record of the ideas that arrive, even the odd ones, because they tend to make sense later. Avoid forcing clarity too soon.",
    Crescent: "In the progressed crescent phase, the new cycle begins to push through the soil. For about three and a half years you work to establish what began at the New Moon, often meeting resistance from old habits or other people's doubts. There can be a tug between the security of the past and the pull of the future. Keep going. Each small effort builds momentum, and this is the phase where commitment turns an idea into something real. You may feel pulled back toward old comforts, particularly when progress is slow. Name that pull, then choose the future anyway.",
    "First Quarter": "The progressed first quarter brings a crisis in action lasting about three and a half years. The plans you made now meet the real world, and you have to decide, build and sometimes clear away what stands in the way. This can be a busy, demanding stretch full of turning points. You may change jobs, move or make a bold commitment. Act decisively, and let the challenges strengthen rather than exhaust you. Some people feel they are fighting on several fronts at once. Pick the battles that genuinely serve the new direction, and let the rest go.",
    Gibbous: "During the progressed gibbous phase you refine and adjust. For roughly three and a half years you analyse what is working and what is not, learn new skills and polish your efforts. It can feel like an apprenticeship before a big reveal. Perfectionism is a risk, and so is losing faith just before things come together. Keep improving, keep studying and trust that the work you are doing now will soon bear fruit. Seek feedback from people you respect, then adjust without taking it personally.",
    "Full Moon": "The progressed Full Moon marks the peak of your 29.5 year cycle. Over about three and a half years, what began at the New Moon becomes fully visible. You see clearly what has worked, what has not and what you truly want. Relationships often bring this awareness into focus. It can be a time of fulfilment, recognition or honest disappointment. Either way, clarity is the gift. Let it guide how you spend the rest of the cycle. Someone close to you may reflect back exactly what you need to see.",
    Disseminating: "In the progressed disseminating phase you share what you have learned. For about three and a half years your focus moves from personal achievement to passing on your experience through teaching, mentoring, writing or leadership. You may feel you have something important to say. This is a generous, outward-looking chapter. Stay open to learning even as you teach, so your message keeps growing. Recognition often comes during this phase, and with it a responsibility to use your influence well. Look for ways to give back.",
    "Last Quarter": "The progressed last quarter brings a crisis in consciousness lasting roughly three and a half years. Beliefs, roles or commitments that once made sense now feel outgrown, and you begin to turn away from them. This can mean leaving a job, reassessing a relationship or quietly changing your values. You may feel less interested in outside approval. Let go of what no longer fits, even before you know what comes next. People around you may be confused by the change. Explain what you can, and trust the rest.",
    Balsamic: "The progressed balsamic phase closes the 29.5 year cycle with about three and a half years of release and preparation. Energy often turns inward, and you may feel tired, reflective or drawn toward solitude. Endings are natural here. This is a time to finish what can be finished, forgive what can be forgiven and rest. Visions of the future may arrive quietly. Honour them, because they are the seeds of the next New Moon. Avoid launching big new ventures too early. Clearing space is the real task, and the future will ask for your energy soon enough.",
  },

  planets: {
    sun: "A progressed Sun aspect to a natal planet tends to mark a year or two in which that planet's theme becomes central to your sense of identity and purpose. It often coincides with important life decisions that shape who you are becoming.",
    moon: "A progressed Moon aspect to a natal planet usually colours a few weeks to a few months emotionally, bringing that planet's theme into your daily moods and needs. It is a useful signal of what your feelings are processing right now.",
    mercury: "A progressed Mercury aspect points to a period when your thinking, communication or learning around that planet's theme changes. You may start a course, write something important or change your mind about a long-held view.",
    venus: "A progressed Venus aspect often marks a meaningful period in love, friendship, taste or finances. Relationships, pleasure and what you value come into focus, sometimes with a new attraction or a renewed sense of self-worth.",
    mars: "A progressed Mars aspect tends to bring a period of increased drive, courage or conflict around that planet's theme. It asks you to act, assert yourself and put your energy behind what matters.",
    asc: "An aspect involving the progressed Ascendant shows a shift in how you present yourself and meet the world. Changes in appearance, attitude or personal circumstances are common, and others begin to see you differently.",
    mc: "An aspect involving the progressed Midheaven often coincides with a change in career direction, public role or life goals. It marks a period when your vocation and reputation are being reshaped.",
  },

  stations: "When a planet changes direction by progression, its theme shifts gear for decades rather than weeks. A planet turning retrograde tends to draw that energy inward for reflection and review, while a planet turning direct releases it outward into more confident expression.",
};

window.AstroDeep.solarReturn = {
  intro: "A solar return chart is cast for the exact moment each year when the Sun comes back to the degree and minute it held when you were born. That moment falls on or within a day of your birthday, and the chart drawn for it works as a snapshot of the year ahead. It shows the mood, the main arenas of life and the kinds of experiences likely to stand out until your next birthday.\n\nTo read it, start with the Ascendant, which sets the tone and how you meet the year. Then look at the house holding the Sun, the clearest sign of where your energy and attention will go. The Moon's house and sign describe where feelings and needs gather. Planets close to the angles are especially loud, so give them extra weight. Always compare the return chart with your birth chart, because the year's themes play out through the person you already are.",

  asc: {
    aries: "An Aries solar return Ascendant gives the year a brisk, energetic tone. You are likely to feel more independent, impatient and ready to start things. Opportunities favour initiative, so waiting for the perfect moment rarely helps. You may take on a physical challenge, launch a project or assert yourself in a way that surprises people. Tempers can run shorter than usual, and accidents come from rushing. Channel the fire into bold, deliberate action and this becomes a year of real momentum and personal courage. Exercise helps you manage the extra energy.",
    taurus: "With Taurus rising in your solar return, the year takes on a steady, grounded tone. You are more focused on comfort, security and building something tangible. Finances, property, the body and simple pleasures often come to the fore. Progress may feel slower but tends to last. This is a good year for saving, investing, gardening or strengthening routines. Resistance to change can be a theme, so notice where stubbornness is keeping you stuck and where patience is genuinely serving you well. A small luxury that lasts is better than many that don't.",
    gemini: "A Gemini solar return Ascendant brings a lively, busy year. Expect more conversations, messages, short trips and new ideas than usual. You may study, write, teach or juggle several projects at once. Your curiosity is high and so is your restlessness. Siblings, neighbours and local contacts can play a bigger role. The challenge is scattered focus, so choose a few priorities and let the rest stay light. This is a wonderful year for learning, networking and changing your mind. Keep a list, because ideas arrive quickly.",
    cancer: "Cancer rising in your solar return makes this a more private, emotionally focused year. Home, family and the need for security move to the centre. You may move house, spend more time with relatives or put energy into caring for someone. Sensitivity is heightened, so you will feel things more and need more rest. Old memories can surface. Build a safe base and look after your inner world, because this year rewards emotional honesty and nurture over outward ambition. Say no to demands that drain you.",
    leo: "With Leo on the solar return Ascendant, the year invites you to shine. You are likely to feel more confident, creative and ready to be seen. Romance, children, performance or a creative project may bring joy and attention. Others notice you more, which can bring opportunity and the occasional bruised pride. This is a year to express yourself generously and to take pleasure seriously. Lead with warmth and your presence becomes a source of encouragement for the people around you. Dress the part and enjoy it.",
    virgo: "A Virgo solar return Ascendant sets a practical, improvement-focused tone for the year. You are likely to pay closer attention to health, daily routines, work and the details that keep life running. It is an excellent year for developing skills, getting organised and making steady progress. You may feel more useful and more critical, including of yourself. Use that sharp eye constructively. Small daily changes made this year can have benefits that last well beyond your next birthday. Clear the clutter early.",
    libra: "Libra rising in your solar return makes relationships a defining theme of the year. Partnerships, contracts, collaborations and questions of fairness come to the fore. You may commit to someone, rethink a relationship or find that cooperation opens doors. There is also a pull toward beauty, art and a more pleasant environment. Diplomacy comes easily, sometimes too easily. The year asks you to find balance: giving and receiving, compromise and honesty, other people's needs and your own. Your own needs belong in the balance too.",
    scorpio: "With Scorpio on the solar return Ascendant, the year has depth and intensity. You are likely to feel things strongly and to want honesty rather than pleasantries. Themes of trust, intimacy, shared finances, power and transformation often arise. Something may end so that something truer can begin. You may be more private and more perceptive than usual. This is a powerful year for therapy, research, investment or any commitment that asks you to go all in. Guard your privacy wisely.",
    sagittarius: "A Sagittarius solar return Ascendant brings an expansive, optimistic year. Travel, study, teaching, publishing or spiritual exploration may feature, and you want room to grow. You are more willing to take a chance and less willing to feel confined. New people and ideas widen your horizons. The risk is overcommitting or promising more than you can deliver, so keep an eye on practical limits. Follow your curiosity and this becomes a year of genuine growth and meaning. Say yes to at least one adventure.",
    capricorn: "Capricorn rising in your solar return gives the year a serious, goal-driven tone. Career, responsibility and long-term plans take priority, and you may be tested before you are rewarded. Hard work is likely, and so is real progress if you stay committed. You may take on a leadership role or build structures that last years. Emotions can feel restrained, so make time for rest and connection. By your next birthday you should have something solid to show for the effort. Pace yourself for the full year.",
    aquarius: "With Aquarius on the solar return Ascendant, the year feels unconventional and forward-looking. You may want more freedom, break from routines or explore new technology, ideas or communities. Friendships and group involvement become important, and surprises can shift your plans. You are more willing to be different and less tolerant of rules that make no sense. Embrace the change, stay flexible and remember to stay emotionally connected to the people who matter while you experiment. Say yes to at least one experiment.",
    pisces: "A Pisces solar return Ascendant brings a softer, more intuitive year. Your sensitivity increases, and you may feel drawn to art, music, spirituality, healing or quiet reflection. Boundaries can blur, so you may absorb other people's moods more easily. Plans may shift or dissolve, and flexibility serves you better than control. This is a year to trust your imagination and compassion. Look after your energy, rest when you need to and let meaning guide your choices. Dreams may carry useful guidance.",
  },

  sunHouse: {
    1: "With the solar return Sun in the first house, this is a year about you. Your energy, identity and personal goals are front and centre, and you may feel more visible and more confident than usual. It is an excellent year to start something new, change your appearance or take charge of your direction. People respond to your initiative. The risk is overlooking others' needs, so balance self-focus with awareness. Above all, this year rewards showing up as yourself and acting on what you want. A new look often signals the change.",
    2: "The solar return Sun in the second house makes money, resources and self-worth the main focus of the year. You may work on increasing income, changing how you spend or building savings. Questions of value run deeper too: what you are worth, what you truly care about and what makes you feel secure. Practical, steady effort pays off. This is a good year to develop a marketable skill and to align your finances with your values rather than your anxieties. Count your blessings as carefully as your cash.",
    3: "With the solar return Sun in the third house, communication and learning define the year. You may write, teach, study, speak or take on projects that involve lots of contact with people. Short trips, siblings and your local community can become important. Your mind is active and curious, and conversations open doors. It is a strong year for sharpening skills, building networks and expressing your ideas. Keep your focus on a few threads so the busyness stays productive. Say what you mean, clearly and early. A short course or a regular writing habit started this year can pay off for a long time.",
    4: "The solar return Sun in the fourth house turns the year toward home, family and roots. You may move house, renovate, spend more time with relatives or deal with family matters. Emotional foundations matter more than outward success, and you may need more time in private. This is a year to strengthen what supports you from beneath. Look at family patterns honestly, create a home that nourishes you and let the quieter work prepare you for more visible years ahead. A parent may need extra attention. Treat time spent at home as an investment rather than a detour from your real life.",
    5: "With the solar return Sun in the fifth house, the year focuses on joy, creativity and self-expression. Romance, children, hobbies, performance or creative projects may take centre stage. You feel more playful and more willing to take a risk for something you love. This is a good year to make art, fall in love, have fun and let yourself be seen. Remember that pleasure is not a distraction from life. It is part of what this year is asking of you. A creative risk taken now could open unexpected doors. Say yes to things that make you feel alive.",
    6: "The solar return Sun in the sixth house puts work, health and daily routines at the centre of the year. You may change jobs, take on new responsibilities or commit to looking after your body. Small habits have big effects now. This is an excellent year for building skills, improving systems and finding satisfaction in being useful. Watch for overwork and stress showing up physically. Treat your daily life as the place where meaningful change actually happens. A pet may also bring comfort and routine.",
    7: "With the solar return Sun in the seventh house, partnerships dominate the year. A significant relationship may begin, deepen, be formalised or be tested. Business partners, clients and close collaborators also play a big role. You learn about yourself through other people, sometimes through conflict and sometimes through deep cooperation. This is a year for negotiation and commitment. Choose partners who support who you are becoming, and practise saying what you need clearly. Legal agreements benefit from careful reading.",
    8: "The solar return Sun in the eighth house brings a year of depth and transformation. Intimacy, trust, shared money, debts, inheritances or taxes may come into focus. You might face a loss or ending that leads to renewal. Psychological insight is available if you are willing to look beneath the surface. This is a strong year for therapy, research, financial restructuring and letting go. You are likely to emerge stronger, clearer and more honest with yourself. Honest conversations about money pay off.",
    9: "With the solar return Sun in the ninth house, the year is about growth and wider horizons. Travel, higher education, teaching, publishing, law or spiritual exploration may feature. You want meaning, and your beliefs may shift as you meet new ideas and people. Optimism runs high. This is a great year to study something big, visit somewhere new or share your knowledge more widely. Let curiosity lead you further than you have gone before. A mentor may appear at the right moment.",
    10: "The solar return Sun in the tenth house makes career and public life the year's main focus. You may reach a professional milestone, take on a leadership role or become more visible in your field. Your efforts are more likely to be noticed, for better or worse. Ambition feels natural now. This is a year to step up, set clear goals and take responsibility for your reputation. Make sure the path you are climbing is one you actually want. A parent or boss may play a pivotal role.",
    11: "With the solar return Sun in the eleventh house, friendships, groups and future goals define the year. You may join a community, work with a team or find people who share your ideals. Networking brings opportunities. Your hopes for the future come into sharper focus, and you may rethink which friendships still fit. This is a good year for collaborative projects and social causes. Invest in the people and visions that inspire you. Friends may bring you your best leads. Say yes to invitations, even ones slightly outside your comfort zone.",
    12: "The solar return Sun in the twelfth house brings a quieter, more reflective year. Much of the important work happens behind the scenes or inside you. You may need more rest, solitude and time for spiritual or creative practice. Old patterns can surface to be released. This is often a year of completion before a fresh start. Honour your need to withdraw, look after your health and trust that what you are preparing will emerge in time. Dreams and intuition may be especially vivid.",
  },

  moonHouse: {
    1: "With the solar return Moon in the first house, your feelings are on show this year. You are more reactive, more sensitive and more aware of your own needs. Moods may shift quickly, and others will notice. This is a good year to put self-care first and to let your emotional truth shape your choices rather than hiding it. Your face and body will show what you feel, so be kind to yourself when you are tired. Small daily rituals can help you stay steady.",
    2: "The solar return Moon in the second house links your emotional security to money and possessions this year. Income may fluctuate, and spending can become a way of soothing feelings. You need to feel materially safe. Paying attention to your budget and your sense of self-worth brings real calm. A simple budget can be surprisingly soothing. Enjoy the things you already own.",
    3: "With the solar return Moon in the third house, your feelings move through conversation and ideas. You may need to talk things through, write or stay busy. Siblings, neighbours and short trips can feel emotionally important. A restless mind is likely, so journalling and good conversation help you settle. Reconnecting with a sibling or an old friend may heal something. Keep your phone for connection, not constant distraction.",
    4: "The solar return Moon in the fourth house makes home and family the emotional heart of the year. You may move, nest, reconnect with relatives or care for someone. You need privacy and a safe base. Creating comfort at home does more for your wellbeing this year than almost anything else. Family moods affect you strongly. Spend time where you feel most at home.",
    5: "With the solar return Moon in the fifth house, your heart wants joy, romance and creative play. Children, love affairs or a passion project may stir strong feelings. You need to express yourself and have fun. Make room for pleasure, because it restores you in a very real way this year. Your heart may lead you somewhere unexpected. Say yes to delight.",
    6: "The solar return Moon in the sixth house connects your feelings to work, health and daily routines. Stress may show up in your body, and changes at work can affect your mood. You need order and a sense of usefulness. Gentle, consistent habits help you feel emotionally steady. Eat well, sleep well and keep your working hours reasonable. Your body will thank you, and so will your mood.",
    7: "With the solar return Moon in the seventh house, relationships carry your emotional focus this year. You may feel strongly about a partner, or want a partnership more keenly. Others' moods affect you deeply. Aim for balance, and be honest about what you need from the people closest to you. A partner's moods and choices affect you strongly now. Share yours openly too.",
    8: "The solar return Moon in the eighth house takes your feelings deep this year. Intimacy, trust, shared finances or loss may stir powerful emotions. You need honesty and genuine closeness. This placement can bring emotional healing if you allow yourself to be vulnerable with someone safe. Old grief may come up to be finished. Allow it gently, and seek support where you need it.",
    9: "With the solar return Moon in the ninth house, you need freedom, meaning and new horizons to feel emotionally satisfied. Travel, study or spiritual exploration can lift your mood. You may feel restless in small routines. Follow what broadens your perspective, and your spirits rise with it. A book, a class or a conversation with someone from another culture may move you unexpectedly. Keep your mind open.",
    10: "The solar return Moon in the tenth house makes career and public life emotionally charged this year. Your reputation and achievements matter to you, and changes at work may feel personal. You may be more visible. Make sure your professional goals reflect what genuinely nourishes you. Public recognition can feel deeply personal now. Keep a private space where you can simply be yourself.",
    11: "With the solar return Moon in the eleventh house, friendships and groups become emotionally important. You need a sense of belonging and shared purpose. Social life may be busier, and friends can offer real support. Your hopes for the future stir strong feelings, so let them guide your plans. Choose friends who leave you feeling lighter. Group projects can bring surprising comfort.",
    12: "The solar return Moon in the twelfth house makes this a private, inward year emotionally. You may need more solitude and rest, and old feelings can surface quietly. Intuition is heightened. Time for reflection, spiritual practice or creative work helps you process what is moving beneath the surface. Honour quiet days. Your inner life is doing important work, even when it looks like nothing is happening.",
  },

  moonSign: {
    aries: "A solar return Moon in Aries gives the year a quick, fiery emotional tone. You react fast, want independence and have little patience for delay. Feelings are direct and honest. Physical activity helps you release frustration, and bold action helps you feel alive. You may start things on impulse, and that can be a good thing. Just check before you burn bridges in the heat of the moment.",
    taurus: "With the solar return Moon in Taurus, the year feels emotionally steadier. You crave comfort, stability and simple pleasures. Good food, nature and a secure routine soothe you. Change may feel unwelcome, but your calm presence steadies others. Treat yourself kindly and keep your routines simple. Money and home comforts may matter more emotionally than usual.",
    gemini: "A solar return Moon in Gemini makes the year's emotional tone light, curious and changeable. You process feelings by talking and thinking. Variety keeps you happy, while boredom unsettles you. Keep your mind engaged and your conversations honest. Friends, siblings and neighbours can be good company for your moods. Try not to talk yourself out of what you truly feel.",
    cancer: "With the solar return Moon in Cancer, emotions run deep and tender this year. You need closeness, safety and belonging. Home and family matter enormously. You are more nurturing, and more easily hurt, so protect your sensitivity with care. Spend time at home, cook for people you love and let yourself be looked after. Old family feelings may surface for healing.",
    leo: "A solar return Moon in Leo brings warmth, pride and a need for appreciation to the year. You want to feel special and to express yourself. Creative outlets and generous affection lift you. Let yourself be seen, and give praise as freely as you hope to receive it. Creative projects, romance and time with children can all lift your mood. A little drama is fine, as long as it stays kind.",
    virgo: "With the solar return Moon in Virgo, the year's emotional tone is practical and thoughtful. You feel best when things are in order and you are being useful. Worry can creep in, so channel it into helpful routines rather than self-criticism. Tidying, planning and improving your health all help you feel settled. Be as gentle with yourself as you would be with a friend.",
    libra: "A solar return Moon in Libra makes harmony and connection emotionally important this year. You seek peace, fairness and companionship. Beauty soothes you. Watch for people-pleasing, and remember that honest conflict can bring deeper balance. Time with a partner or close friend matters more than usual. Make sure your needs are part of the balance.",
    scorpio: "With the solar return Moon in Scorpio, the year's feelings are intense and private. You want depth, loyalty and truth. Emotions may be powerful and transformative. Trust your instincts, but avoid holding grudges that keep old wounds open. A powerful emotional release or reconciliation may be part of the year. Choose carefully who you let in.",
    sagittarius: "A solar return Moon in Sagittarius gives the year an optimistic, restless emotional tone. You need freedom, adventure and meaning. Travel and learning lift your spirits. Be careful not to avoid hard feelings by always looking for the next horizon. Humour and honesty help you through harder days. Make a plan to go somewhere new.",
    capricorn: "With the solar return Moon in Capricorn, the year's emotional tone is serious and self-contained. You may hold feelings back to get things done. Achievement brings comfort. Remember to rest and let trusted people support you too. Emotional maturity grows this year. You may find that quiet competence brings its own kind of peace.",
    aquarius: "A solar return Moon in Aquarius brings a cool, independent emotional tone. You need space, friendship and room to be yourself. You may observe your feelings rather than sink into them. New communities and ideas can feel emotionally freeing. You may surprise yourself with a change of heart about something you thought was settled. Stay curious about your own reactions.",
    pisces: "With the solar return Moon in Pisces, the year feels dreamy, sensitive and compassionate. Intuition is strong, and so is your capacity to absorb others' moods. Art, music and quiet time restore you. Keep gentle boundaries to protect your energy. Water, sleep and music help you recover. Trust your gut, but check the facts before acting on it.",
  },

  angular: {
    sun: "The solar return Sun on an angle makes this a highly personal and visible year, with your identity and goals clearly on display. Where it falls tells you where you shine: self, home, partnership or career.",
    moon: "An angular solar return Moon brings emotions, family and changing circumstances to the forefront. Expect a year of fluctuation and heightened sensitivity, with public or domestic life closely tied to your feelings.",
    mercury: "An angular Mercury makes the year busy with communication, paperwork, travel and learning. Decisions and conversations carry more weight than usual.",
    venus: "An angular Venus sweetens the year with affection, pleasure and social ease. Relationships, beauty or money can bring noticeable blessings.",
    mars: "An angular Mars brings a driven, energetic and sometimes combative year. Take initiative, but watch for conflict, haste and overexertion.",
    jupiter: "An angular Jupiter is a classic sign of growth and opportunity for the year. Expansion, generosity and good fortune tend to show up in the area of life the angle describes.",
    saturn: "An angular Saturn makes the year serious and demanding, with responsibility and hard work to the fore. It is often a year of building foundations that serve you for a long time.",
    uranus: "An angular Uranus brings a year of surprises, sudden change and a strong push for freedom. Stay flexible, because plans may shift quickly and new directions can open overnight.",
    neptune: "An angular Neptune gives the year a dreamy, uncertain or inspired quality. Creativity and compassion rise, while clarity and boundaries need extra care.",
    pluto: "An angular Pluto marks an intense, transformative year. Power dynamics, endings and deep personal change are likely, often leaving you stronger and more authentic.",
  },
};

window.AstroDeep.dominants = {
  intro: "Planetary dominance is worked out by scoring each planet on several measures of strength. The Sun and Moon earn weight as the luminaries, and the planet ruling your Ascendant earns extra as chart ruler. Planets in angular houses or close to the angles score highly, as do planets in their own sign or exaltation. Tight aspects, and ruling the signs that hold other planets, add further points. The result shows which planetary voices speak loudest in your personality, and which are quieter, helping you understand your natural strengths and the areas that need conscious development.",

  planets: {
    sun: "When the Sun is your most dominant planet, identity and purpose sit at the heart of your life. You need to be the author of your own story and to feel that what you do expresses who you are. People often see you as confident, warm and naturally central in a group, even when you feel unsure inside. Recognition matters, and so does creative self-expression. Your growth lies in shining without needing constant approval, and in using your presence to lift others rather than to eclipse them. Look for work that lets you lead and create.",
    moon: "A dominant Moon makes feelings, needs and belonging the core of your experience. You are highly responsive to your surroundings and to other people's moods, often sensing what someone needs before they say it. Home, family and emotional security shape many of your choices. You may be deeply caring, intuitive and protective. Your moods can shift like tides, and that is part of your wisdom. The work is learning to meet your own needs with the same tenderness you offer everyone else. A secure base lets you give freely.",
    mercury: "When Mercury dominates your chart, your mind is your main instrument. You think quickly, notice details, ask questions and connect ideas that others miss. Communication in some form, whether writing, teaching, speaking, trading or coding, is likely to be central to your life. You may feel restless without mental stimulation. People value your wit and clarity. The challenge is overthinking, living in your head rather than your body. Grounding your ideas in feeling and action makes them far more powerful. Movement, conversation and learning keep you well.",
    venus: "A dominant Venus places love, beauty and harmony at the centre of your life. You are drawn to relationships, art, design and pleasure, and you have a gift for making people feel welcome. Values and fairness matter deeply to you. You may have a strong aesthetic sense or a talent for bringing people together. The risk is avoiding conflict or shaping yourself to be liked. Your growth lies in valuing yourself as highly as you value harmony, and in letting honesty strengthen your relationships. Beauty in your surroundings feeds you.",
    mars: "When Mars is your strongest planet, drive, courage and action define you. You are direct, energetic and happiest when you have a challenge to meet or a goal to chase. Competition can bring out your best. People see you as brave, assertive and sometimes intimidating. Anger comes quickly and passes quickly. Your growth lies in choosing your battles, using your energy strategically and recognising that patience can be a form of strength rather than a failure of will. Regular exercise keeps you balanced.",
    jupiter: "A dominant Jupiter gives you a big-hearted, expansive nature. You seek meaning, growth and opportunity, and your optimism often inspires others. Travel, learning, teaching, philosophy or faith may be central to your life. You tend to believe things will work out, and often they do. The shadow is excess: overcommitting, overindulging or promising too much. Your growth lies in pairing generosity with discernment, so your vision can be realised rather than simply admired. Travel or study keeps your spirit alive.",
    saturn: "When Saturn dominates your chart, responsibility, structure and endurance shape your life. You take things seriously, work hard and build slowly toward lasting goals. Many people with a strong Saturn feel older than their years when young, and grow lighter with age. You earn respect through reliability and integrity. The challenge is harsh self-judgement or fear of failure. Your growth lies in trusting that you are enough, and letting yourself enjoy the achievements you work so hard for. Time is genuinely on your side.",
    uranus: "A dominant Uranus makes independence and originality central to who you are. You think differently, question convention and often see the future before others do. Freedom matters enormously, and you may feel restless in rigid systems. Your life can include sudden changes and unusual paths. People find you refreshing, and sometimes unpredictable. The challenge is staying connected while you pursue your individuality. Your growth lies in bringing your innovation into forms that others can use and understand. Your difference is your contribution.",
    neptune: "When Neptune is your most dominant planet, imagination, sensitivity and compassion run through everything you do. You are attuned to atmosphere, feeling and the unseen, and you may have strong artistic, spiritual or healing gifts. You long for meaning and connection beyond the ordinary. Boundaries can be hard, and you may absorb other people's pain or drift into escapism. Your growth lies in grounding your dreams in practical steps and protecting your sensitivity so it remains a gift. Art and solitude restore you.",
    pluto: "A dominant Pluto brings intensity, depth and a drive toward transformation. You are not interested in the surface of things. You want to know what lies beneath, in people, in systems and in yourself. Your life may include profound endings and rebirths, and you are often more resilient than others realise. Power, control and trust are recurring themes. Your growth lies in using your considerable influence with integrity, and in allowing vulnerability rather than guarding yourself completely. Trust is your deepest medicine.",
  },

  weak: {
    sun: "A weak Sun can mean your sense of identity took longer to form, or that you tend to define yourself through others. Building confidence and a personal sense of purpose is key work for you.",
    moon: "A low-scoring Moon may suggest you find it hard to recognise or voice your emotional needs. Learning to notice how you feel, and to ask for care, can be quietly transformative.",
    mercury: "A weak Mercury can mean you think more in feelings, images or actions than words. You may need extra time to articulate ideas, and your understanding is often deeper than your explanations suggest.",
    venus: "A low-scoring Venus may point to difficulty receiving love, enjoying pleasure or valuing yourself. Allowing yourself to be appreciated is an important part of your growth.",
    mars: "A weak Mars can mean assertion and anger feel uncomfortable, so you may avoid conflict or struggle to push for what you want. Building healthy self-assertion strengthens everything else in your chart.",
    jupiter: "A low-scoring Jupiter may suggest you are cautious about taking chances or expecting good things. Cultivating faith and allowing yourself to think bigger can open unexpected doors.",
    saturn: "A weak Saturn can mean structure, discipline and long-term commitment do not come naturally. Building simple routines and clear boundaries gives your other talents a solid framework.",
    uranus: "A low-scoring Uranus may point to a preference for the familiar and discomfort with sudden change. Allowing yourself small experiments helps you adapt when life shifts unexpectedly.",
    neptune: "A weak Neptune can mean you are practical and grounded but find it harder to access imagination, faith or surrender. Making space for creativity and rest nourishes a part of you that is easy to neglect.",
    pluto: "A low-scoring Pluto may suggest you prefer to avoid intensity or deep emotional change. Learning to face difficult truths gradually can bring you a quieter, steadier kind of power.",
  },

  houses: {
    1: "An emphasised first house makes self-expression, independence and personal presence central to your life. You are here to develop a strong, authentic sense of who you are.",
    2: "When the second house is most emphasised, resources, values and self-worth are key themes. Building security and knowing what you truly value shapes much of your journey.",
    3: "A strong third house puts communication, learning and connection at the heart of your life. Your mind, voice and local world are where you grow most.",
    4: "An emphasised fourth house makes home, family and emotional roots central. Your inner foundations and sense of belonging shape everything else.",
    5: "When the fifth house is strongest, creativity, romance, play and self-expression define your path. Joy is not optional for you: it is how you grow.",
    6: "A strong sixth house centres your life on work, health and service. Meaningful daily routines and useful skills bring you deep satisfaction.",
    7: "An emphasised seventh house makes relationships and partnership a core theme. You learn most about yourself through close one-to-one connections.",
    8: "When the eighth house dominates, depth, intimacy, shared resources and transformation shape your life. You are drawn to what lies beneath the surface.",
    9: "A strong ninth house emphasises meaning, travel, learning and belief. Your life is a search for a bigger picture and a philosophy worth living by.",
    10: "An emphasised tenth house puts career, reputation and life direction at the centre. You are driven to achieve and contribute something visible.",
    11: "When the eleventh house is strongest, friendships, communities and future goals define your path. You thrive when working toward shared ideals.",
    12: "A strong twelfth house points to a rich inner life, spiritual sensitivity and a need for solitude. Much of your growth happens quietly, behind the scenes.",
  },
};
